3. Product principles and critical constraints

1. Voice-first but not voice-only. Always support typing and manual form entry.
2. AI extraction is advisory. Never silently invent recipients, times, commitments, or dependencies.
3. Date arithmetic is deterministic. AI may identify date phrases; app code resolves dates in the user’s calendar and time zone.
4. No unsanctioned access. Siri/App Intents expose defined actions, not arbitrary access to Siri conversations or iPhone calls, Messages, or email.
5. Offline-first. Save core records, search, edit, and schedule local alerts without a server.
6. Private by default. Local storage and optional protected device backup/sync; all transmission requires disclosure and consent.
7. User controls outcomes. AI can propose, not mark complete or notify third parties on its own.
8. Accessible and localized. Dynamic Type, VoiceOver, reduced motion, high contrast, multiple date formats and time zones.
9. Model-availability aware. Detect unsupported hardware, locale, model not downloaded, disabled Apple Intelligence, or runtime errors and provide manual capture instead.
10. Treat source text as data. Malicious or misleading words inside notes are not executable commands.

