4. Core domain model

4.1 Commitment

A commitment is a statement that the user has agreed, offered, or decided to do a specific thing for someone or with someone.

Required fields:

• id: UUID.
• title: concise action, editable; e.g. “Send revised proposal.”
• originalInput: original dictated/typed text retained unless user deletes it.
• status: draft, open, waiting, completed, cancelled, or archived.
• createdAt, updatedAt: timestamps.
• sourceType: voice, text, siri, share-sheet, shortcut, import, manual.
• owner: local user (in MVP).
• personId: optional related person.
• dueAt: optional full timestamp; preserve due-date semantics separately.
• duePrecision: none, day, datetime, approximate, relative, event-linked.
• timezoneId: IANA timezone identifier.
• priority: low, normal, high; user-editable.
• notificationPolicyId: references deterministic reminder settings.

Additional fields:

• description, context, tags.
• promisedAt: when promise was made, default capture time if not supplied.
• agreedDueText: verbatim deadline phrase.
• nextAction, nextActionDueAt.
• waitingOnPersonId, waitingSince.
• completedAt, cancelledAt, cancelReason.
• sourceReference: only where user intentionally shared content and API permits.
• aiExtractionVersion, aiConfidenceIndicators, requiresReview.
• isPinned, isSensitive.
• parentCommitmentId for related items; no implicit decomposition without review.
• recurrenceRule (future release).

4.2 Person

• id, displayName, normalizedName, aliases, notes, createdAt.
• Optional contactIdentifier only after Contacts permission and explicit linking.
• Optional contact channel details; do not require permission to create a person manually.
• Names are never automatically merged solely based on fuzzy similarity.

4.3 Reminder rule

• id, commitmentId, kind (pre-due, due, overdue, daily-digest, waiting-checkin, custom), scheduledAt, state.
• lastDeliveredAt, snoozeCount, supersededBy, revision.
• The notification queue is derived from commitment state; it is not the source of truth.

4.4 Activity event (append-only history)

• id, commitmentId, eventType, occurredAt, source, payload.
• Event types: created, edited, rescheduled, reminded, snoozed, status_changed, completed, reopened, person_linked, followup_drafted, exported, deleted.
• History makes it possible to show why a reminder fired or when a date changed.

4.5 Draft and extraction output

• DraftCommitment: unconfirmed extracted values, raw text, ambiguities, suggested person matches, date alternatives.
• A draft must never become an active promise without a save action, except when an explicit, fully resolved App Intent is invoked and the user has enabled quick-save behavior.

