6. Functional requirements

FR-01 Capture — P0

Input modes: text entry, in-app microphone, Siri/App Shortcut (defined intent), share sheet for user-shared text (P1). Action button shortcut should open capture or invoke defined capture intent where available.

• Capture control visible from all primary screens.
• Transcript editable before extraction and before save.
• Multiple extraction supported, with separate review cards.
• Cancel must discard unsaved records after confirmation if substantive edits exist.
• Background/locked-screen Siri flows must degrade gracefully to opening the app when interactive review is needed.
• No covert recording or background microphone surveillance.

FR-02 AI structured interpretation — P0

Extract:

• Promise count and boundaries.
• Proposed action title and description.
• People named and candidate matches.
• When promise was made, due date phrase and due-time precision.
• Dependencies, waiting state and requested next step.
• Priority signals only when explicit or strongly supported.
• Evidence spans from the original text for auditable fields.
• Explicit unknown/ambiguous markers.

Rules:

• Use guided generation (@Generable/structured types) with Foundation Models, subject to deployed SDK API availability.
• Model output passes strict validation and domain normalization.
• No recipient inferred from prior context without showing it as suggestion.
• No default due date magically created for undated commitments.
• Locale-specific dates resolved in code, not by trusting free-text generation alone.
• Do not promise a numeric model confidence score that is statistically calibrated; use field validation and ambiguity rules.
• No model access must block manual fallback.

FR-03 People — P0

• Create, rename, merge (explicitly), archive local people.
• Associate multiple commitments with a person.
• Search names and aliases.
• Suggestions for already stored people are reviewable.
• No Contacts permission necessary.
• Optional Contacts read/link integration only in P1, with minimal scope.

FR-04 Dates and deadlines — P0

• Date-only and exact-time commitments supported.
• Distinguish hard deadlines from approximate periods (“next week”).
• Ambiguous utterances show a clear resolution request.
• Relative dates computed from timestamp, locale/calendar and time zone.
• Handle DST changes, past dates, travel/time-zone switches and editing.
• A due date may remain empty; unscheduled promises live in a distinct inbox.
• User can reschedule; every reschedule logs old/new values.

FR-05 Notifications — P0

• Local user notifications after permission is granted.
• User-configurable reminders: day-before, hour-before, at-due, overdue, per-item custom.
• Daily digest opt-in, no duplicates.
• Notification actions: Done, Snooze, Open (as supported).
• Pending notifications updated/cancelled on edit, complete, delete, or reschedule.
• Respect OS focus/quiet behavior; do not claim delivery is guaranteed at exact time.
• Handle pending-request limits by prioritizing near-term reminders and replenishing the schedule at reliable app execution points. Do not depend on exact periodic background execution.
• If notifications denied, display clear in-app reminder status and route to Settings, but keep app usable.

FR-06 Commitment lists and detail — P0

Tabs: Today, Upcoming, People, History, Settings, with floating universal capture button. Support smart filters: Overdue, Today, This week, Waiting, Unscheduled, Completed.

Commitment detail:

• Large outcome/action title, person, due date, current status, next action, source transcription, notes, reminder plan, activity timeline.
• Edit, mark done, snooze, reschedule, switch to waiting, cancel, duplicate, delete.
• Show exact reason when the app says overdue.
• Preserve edit history without making the interface overwhelming.

FR-07 Search — P0

• Search title, description, people, notes, tags.
• Offline indexed search, case/diacritic tolerant where supported.
• Filter by status and date interval.
• Natural-language semantic queries are P1 and must degrade to keyword/filter search.

FR-08 Siri and Shortcuts — P0

Implement App Intents and App Shortcuts for:

|Intent        |Parameters                                                     |Behavior                                     |
|--------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
|Add Promise   |natural language text or structured title; optional person/date|Extract or save, with review if uncertain    |
|Show Promises |optional person/status/date filter                             |Return short summary or open list            |
|Mark Complete |commitment entity identifier                                   |Mark exactly one resolved commitment complete|
|Snooze Promise|commitment identifier and duration                             |Adjust next notification; log event          |
|Open Capture  |none                                                           |Open app directly into capture UI            |

Use AppEntity, entity queries, stable identifiers, phrase examples, localized display names, intent donations, and AppShortcutsProvider as appropriate. Siri examples must use the app name in eligible phrases; third-party phrase recognition and follow-up conversations are OS-controlled and are not guaranteed.

Use an app-group-safe storage interface or another correct cross-process persistence mechanism if app extensions/widgets are present. Ensure intents can access the same source of truth and return only after persistence succeeds.

FR-09 Briefing — P1

• Today/next-7-days overview; overdue and waiting categories.
• Configurable daily notification and on-demand Siri summary.
• AI can generate a concise optional narrative, but facts and counts come from deterministic queries.
• Never imply another person has actually been contacted.

FR-10 Follow-up drafts — P1

• “Draft an apology for being late” or “Draft a project status update to Anna.”
• Generate editable text locally; provide system share sheet/copy options.
• User must explicitly choose/send the destination; no silent messages or emails.
• App does not claim message was sent unless an authorized integration reports success.

FR-11 Apple Reminders interoperability — P1

• Optional export to Apple Reminders using EventKit with permission.
• Clear directionality and ownership: app is source of truth; avoid two-way sync in MVP.
• Explicit user action to create or update entries.
• Track external identifier and errors; do not silently duplicate reminders.

FR-12 Sync and backup — P1

• Optional iCloud/CloudKit private-zone sync across user’s devices with compatible entitlement and account.
• Offline change queue, conflict policy and deletion tombstones.
• Separate local-device-only mode.
• Export all data as JSON/CSV, import, and delete-all capabilities.
• Restore tests, encryption/data-protection and conflict resolution required before feature release.

FR-13 Accessibility and localization — P0

• Dynamic Type up to accessibility sizes; VoiceOver controls fully named.
• Color is not the only status signal; strong contrast, reduced motion.
• Voice control and hardware keyboard support.
• Ship English initially; architect strings and date parsing for Polish support. Do not imply local AI language support without runtime check.
• Support 12/24-hour formats and regional week starts.

