10. Notification scheduling rules

Default policy is configurable and deliberately conservative:

1. Exact timestamp due: schedule an alert at due time and optional advance reminder(s).
2. Date-only due: use user’s configurable preferred reminder time; ask/set this in settings, not an unexplained midnight alert.
3. Approximate due: propose a check-in, never invent a hard due timestamp.
4. No due date: keep in Unscheduled, optional weekly review.
5. Waiting: user-selected check-in cadence, never falsely mark overdue.
6. Completed/cancelled: remove all future notifications.
7. Snoozed: reschedule according to explicit snooze choice while preserving original due date.
8. Overdue: show in Overdue until status changes; notifications should not spam repeatedly.

At app foreground launch, after persistence mutation, and when reliable OS callbacks occur, reconcile desired future reminders with pending delivered/scheduled OS notifications. OS scheduling/Focus behavior means precise delivery cannot be guaranteed.

