12. Metrics and instrumentation

Collect privacy-preserving aggregate events, strictly avoiding commitment text, person identities and transcript payloads.

Activation:

• Percent completing a first saved promise within day 1.
• Median time from opening capture to saving first item.
• Percent needing manual fixes after extraction.

Engagement:

• WAU/MAU.
• Weekly new commitments per active user.
• Share captured via voice, Siri and typed entry.
• Completion rate before/at/after due date.
• Overdue commitments resolved per week.

Retention and business:

• Week-1 and week-4 retention.
• Free-to-paid conversion and trial conversion (if trials are used).
• Paid subscriber churn and annual renewal.
• Support tickets per 100 active users.

Trust:

• “Wrong reminder” reports.
• AI invented promise reports.
• User correction rates and date ambiguities.
• Notifications permission denial rate.

Suggested early goals (hypotheses to validate): median first capture <20 seconds including review; 40% week-4 retention among activated users; fewer than 1% of reviewed extractions reported as an invented promise; paid conversion target 3–5% after acquisition and retention analysis.

