14. Edge cases and error states

1. Wrong direction: “Sarah promised me a quote” is not silently interpreted as a user-owned commitment.
2. Negation: “I did not promise to send it” produces no active promise.
3. Hypothetical: “I might tell Alex I’ll help” is not a confirmed promise.
4. No recipient: User may keep an unassigned personal obligation; request person only if needed.
5. Duplicate capture: Similar text/person/date shows a non-blocking duplicate review.
6. Ambiguous person: Two “Alex” contacts requires choosing a person or leaving unresolved.
7. Ambiguous time: “At 4” needs local assumption or confirmation clearly displayed.
8. Missed deadline in past: Present warning; never auto-complete or silently move it.
9. Timezone change: Preserve user-intended calendar/date semantics separately from absolute notification time; recalculate explicitly.
10. DST transition: No invalid/nonexistent scheduled local time.
11. Denied speech permission: Typing always works.
12. Model unavailable or busy: Show reason and usable manual fallback.
13. Notification permissions denied: Promises still stored; prominent in-app status.
14. Device low storage: Save transaction fails cleanly with actionable message.
15. Duplicate Siri invocation: Idempotent creation token where feasible; avoid duplicate writes on retries.
16. Deleted person: Associated commitments should preserve meaningful historical display; explicit reassignment option.
17. Partial multi-promise save: Confirm which draft(s) succeeded, retain unsaved drafts, no duplicated saves.
18. Interrupted recording: Recover any already transcribed text and allow retry/discard.
19. AI prompt injection in dictated text: Treat as quoted data, not system instructions.
20. Subscription expiry: Existing records remain accessible and exportable.

