15. Test strategy

Unit tests

• Date resolver with time zones, DST, week boundaries, leap years, locale variants.
• Status transition rules and idempotency.
• Notification policy generation and reconciliation.
• People matching/duplicate suggestions.
• Subscription entitlement gating.
• Manual capture and schema validation.

AI contract tests

• At least 250 curated examples, including noisy dictation, ambiguity, negation, multiple promises, and adversarial text.
• Strict schema decoding and validator failure tests.
• Model disabled/unavailable tests and fallback UI tests.
• Golden tests for known extraction regressions.

Integration tests

• Save → relaunch → record persists.
• Siri App Intent creates exactly one item; can retrieve and complete it.
• Notification action marks correct item and cancels future reminders.
• Edit date → previous scheduled reminder removed and new one installed.
• Reinstall/backup/restore behavior documented and verified to the extent the chosen storage architecture supports it.
• StoreKit local configuration and sandbox renewals/cancellations.

UI/accessibility tests

• VoiceOver for capture/edit/completion.
• Dynamic Type and dark mode.
• Permission denial and settings recovery flows.
• Onboarding skip, zero records, thousands of records, long names and long transcripts.

Device matrix

• At least one iPhone supporting selected Apple Intelligence profile and one unsupported device or simulated unavailable state.
• English launch locale, Polish test locale if Polish is enabled.
• Airplane mode, poor battery/network, Siri enabled/disabled.
• The app must not depend on Swift Playgrounds or the simulator to validate Siri, speech, notifications, or StoreKit: test on physical devices.

