16. Delivery phases and exit gates

Phase 0 — technical proof

• Validate Foundation Models availability and guided extraction on actual target devices.
• Validate speech transcription support for launch locales.
• Implement one App Intent with a real saved item and Siri invocation on device.
• Prove local notifications schedule and update after app relaunch.

Exit: Video/manual test evidence of end-to-end speak → structured preview → save → reminder → completion, plus working no-model fallback.

Phase 1 — full MVP

• Data model and migrations; capture/edit/list/person/history/search; reminder policy engine; Siri intents; offline fallback; settings; accessibility; core tests.

Exit: No blockers in critical paths; all P0 acceptance scenarios pass on device; no data-loss regressions; privacy policy ready.

Phase 2 — monetized App Store release

• StoreKit subscription UI, entitlement/restore, analytics with privacy boundaries, onboarding polish, diagnostics, subscriptions/App Store metadata and TestFlight review.

Exit: Purchase/restore/expiry scenarios pass; reviewer can use core app with no payment and no Apple Intelligence; App Review assets and links complete.

Phase 3 — retention expansion

• Daily briefing, follow-up draft composer, widgets, optional Contacts linking/Reminders export, optional iCloud sync, localization and possibly Apple Watch.

Exit: Feature-specific security, integration, migrations, accessibility and QA gates pass.

